         "keepAlive": unknown, // If not specified, the default settings of the client will be used.
         "timeout": 0, // request timeout in milliseconds, defaults to client setting
         "query": {},
         "headers": {},
         "signal": AbortSignal // AbortSignal object for cancelling the request
     }
     ```
     Default is {}, no additional information
     @param url Specify url, must be a complete url containing the host
     @param opts Specify additional information
     @return Return HttpRequest object (listen 'response' event to receive the response)
     */
    static HttpRequest head(String url, Object opts = {});

    /*! @brief Request the specified url with HEAD method, register callback to receive response, return HttpRequest object
     @param url Specify url, must be a complete url containing the host
     @param opts Specify additional information
     @param callback Response callback function, receives HttpResponse as parameter
     @return Return HttpRequest object
     */
    static HttpRequest head(String url, Object opts, Function callback);

    /*! @brief Request the specified url with HEAD method, register callback to receive response, return HttpRequest object
     @param url Specify url, must be a complete url containing the host
     @param callback Response callback function, receives HttpResponse as parameter
     @return Return HttpRequest object
     */
    static HttpRequest head(String url, Function callback);

    /*! @brief Dynamically configure proxy support from environment variables for http and https requests
     When invoked, reads proxy configuration from environment variables (HTTP_PROXY, HTTPS_PROXY, NO_PROXY and their lowercase variants)
     and applies them globally. Can be used to enable proxy support dynamically at runtime as an alternative to --use-env-proxy flag.
     
     @param proxyEnv Object containing proxy configuration. If not provided, will read from process.env.
              Supported properties: HTTP_PROXY, http_proxy, HTTPS_PROXY, https_proxy, NO_PROXY, no_proxy
     @return A function that can be called to restore the original proxy configuration
     */
    static Function setGlobalProxyFromEnv(Object proxyEnv = {});

    /*! @brief Send a request using Web Fetch standard and return an HttpResponse
     @param url The request target URL
     @param opts Request options, supports method, headers, body, etc.
     @return Returns an HttpResponse object
    */
    static HttpResponse fetch(String url, Object opts = {}) async;

    /*! @brief Send a Fetch request using an HttpRequest object as the request source, return HttpResponse
     opts may override fields from the request object, supports the following content:
     ```JavaScript
     {
         "method": "GET", // override the method in the request object
         "headers": {}, // merged with request.headers; opts headers override request headers with the same name
         "body": SeekableStream | Buffer | String | {}, // override request.body
         "keepAlive": unknown, // override connection keep-alive setting
         "timeout": 0, // request timeout in milliseconds, defaults to client setting
         "redirect": "follow", // redirect mode: "follow" (default) | "error" | "manual"
         "signal": AbortSignal, // AbortSignal object for cancelling the request
         "streaming": false // whether to return the response body as a stream
     }
     ```
     body, json, pack must not appear at the same time. Default is {}, no fields in request are overridden
     @param request Source request object, provides url, method, headers, body and other base information
     @param opts Specify additional information, may override corresponding fields in request
     @return Return server response, includes status, headers, body, ok, redirected, url, type properties
     */
    static HttpResponse fetch(HttpRequest request, Object opts = {}) async;
};